<speak>The pauses have helped. I dislike being put on a loudspeaker while someone searches for information, because I cannot tell whether they are speaking to me or to a colleague. This has felt more like an ordinary conversation. I would also rather say that I cannot find a page than have someone keep referring to it while I pretend to follow. I was brought up to be polite about inconveniences, and sometimes that creates a larger inconvenience.</speak>